<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n93802" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σημάν-τωρ</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ορος</span>,
			ὁ, (<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σημαίνω</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					11
				</span></i>
			) <i>one who gives a signal, leader, commander</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				4.431
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				19.314
			</span></i>; of a horse, <i>driver</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				8.127
			</span></i>; of a herd, <i>herdsman</i>, <i><span class="en">
				15.325
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Q.S.
				13.74
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θεῶν ς.</span>, of Zeus, <i><span class="en">
				Hes.
				<u>Sc.</u>
				56
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ς. ἄνδρες</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>h.Ap.</u>
					542
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐθνέων ἦσαν ἄλλοι ς.</span>,
			of the <i>subordinate officers</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				7.81
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>informer, guide</i>, <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>OT</u>
				957
			</span></i> (
				v.l.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σημήνας</span>
			)<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">; παγίδων σημάντορα φελλόν</span>
			<i>indicator</i> of the nets, <i><span class="en">
				<u>AP</u>
				6.27
			</span></i> (<i><span class="en">
				Theaet.
			</span></i>); <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μόλιβον, σελίδων ς.
			πλευρῆς</span> (v. 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σελίς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					11
				</span></i>
			), ib.<i><span class="en">
				62
			</span></i> (<i><span class="en">
				Phil.
			</span></i>), cf. <i><span class="en">
				64
			</span></i> (Paul. Sil.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			later as Adj., even in fem., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σημάντορι φωνῇ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Nonn.
					<u>D.</u>
					37.551
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ς. καπνῷ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Tryph.
					237
				</span></i>
			.</div>
